#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166589 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "4dac81da-f15c-55ff-9630-7349a3e03e57" :question/math-academy-id "e-8273" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials $p_1(t)$ and $p_2(t),$ given by\n\n$$\np_1(t)=3+2t, \\qquad\n\tp_2(t)=-t+t^2.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $\\mathcal{B}=\\big\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are ![](images/9e/9eca81c24ee88a63d1c5468160a118cb1e987793d5fdc8d2d7eaa317fadeda93.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n![](images/8c/8c3fce8e9d7cc170ad66706e783c4a46ba0530c119b8b824a66d9b5850e62760.svg)\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =4\\cdot (3+2t)+(-3)\\cdot (-t+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12+8t+3t-3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =12+11t-3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166590 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/id #uuid "aac4b559-b26b-57b0-8701-b3235969cd2f" :question/math-academy-id "e-8274" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n![](images/b9/b9a1cb7eb2a3bcbadd73a68f9e73914e124a2359b8f8fc1ccc33ca950e714f88.svg)\nIf $\\mathcal B = \\{B_1,B_2\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ B_1, B_2 \\},$ calculate ![](images/9b/9b978860f45e9e62e0315727c8eafac13360f29a7762480103b087ed6babf376.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 B_1 +x_2 B_2 = A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](images/88/88ea80808ca87358b78cf322c8ddd81ad7f95ddc02526361aace1ca9b914d486.svg)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 18 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} &=18 \\\\ -{x}_{2} &=-9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get $x_2 =9.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-9 & =-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, ![](images/c5/c57b6f1ce1762add9b5b5d3e15a6363f009482b12b12366434c090d6a7478c6b.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166591 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/id #uuid "f0fc412f-8276-5876-a509-4f2173396e72" :question/math-academy-id "e-8275" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\np_1(t)=5+t^2, \\quad\np_2(t)=3t-2t^2, \\quad\nq(t)=5-3t+3t^2.\n$$\n\nIf $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\},$ find $[q(t)]_{\\mathcal{B}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 p_1(t)+x_2 p_2(t) = q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(5+{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(3t-2{t}^{2}) & =5-3t+3{t}^{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}t+({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =5-3t+3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1} &=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](images/27/271f2b051a53f7aeae9a20ef23b97c9c903a7815f228dfa3ee23e2207bd24ee9.svg)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{5}){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1} &=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first and second equations, we get $x_1=1$ and $x_2 =-1.$ Therefore, ![](images/1f/1fc60fff97ff92bd1cc515e6c984fbacb435dcf0fae24e751842eb8daf3390e8.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243941 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15301301-2403-50d4-a624-ab391b2dc478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241363} {:answer/id #uuid "376486a2-8e17-5715-a7ad-737fa78c1258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241667} {:answer/id #uuid "48d12868-f91f-5e4d-be31-2ca61761e838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241840} {:answer/id #uuid "7d679e70-9da7-5202-a81d-707bd1efa619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242278} {:answer/id #uuid "8468e60b-9874-537b-9d9b-53bca61026d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15301301-2403-50d4-a624-ab391b2dc478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241363} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd008c33-82db-5fa0-8507-c0d8e860acf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33e006b4-f466-5a45-99fb-a4284803e97a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106738" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1+t+{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1+t-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =(-1)\\cdot (1+t+{t}^{2})+1\\cdot (1+t-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-1-t-{t}^{2}+1+t-{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b7570ab-fd63-531d-8e02-29bf746ab1db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559280} {:answer/id #uuid "933e3d56-7dd8-5f4b-8baf-cfed5b9e1537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559382} {:answer/id #uuid "9580e7d9-2197-512f-98b3-2771aef78be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559388} {:answer/id #uuid "9baad326-2a3f-5a1a-891d-cfc23346b6ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559411} {:answer/id #uuid "c2dcc144-7c34-56a2-8495-45807a3fe82c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2dcc144-7c34-56a2-8495-45807a3fe82c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559496} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dd1c54a-c831-5cbe-8eef-ef06db6fc42c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ade0c9c-871d-5f78-8adc-bcd701d0727a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106750" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 & 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-10 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -20 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -20\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-10 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}=-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second  equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-4.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2(-4) & =-10 \\\\ -{x}_{1} & =-2 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2+(-4)=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "128ce6e3-dc22-5943-ae78-9ca654be08a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482842} {:answer/id #uuid "48750a06-11eb-5111-88f7-360fb2f33835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482941} {:answer/id #uuid "5a757e57-8827-5bbe-9ac1-63a3f529a76c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482969} {:answer/id #uuid "87819992-b54e-5a67-ad9b-1e74d374d74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483048} {:answer/id #uuid "b0025512-e99f-5297-ba08-5bbf9b2b1291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a757e57-8827-5bbe-9ac1-63a3f529a76c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482969} :answer-field/id #uuid "d571972e-d66f-51ff-ad55-ae539c035701" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4795a7a-dbd7-5cec-b948-e685d7225538" :question/math-academy-id "q-106778" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{B}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ then $2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & 3{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} &=9 \\\\ -{x}_{1} &=-2 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}↔{R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} &=9 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ -4{x}_{2} &=-12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second,  third and fourth equations, we get ${x}_{2}=3.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3 & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, $2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2\\cdot 2+3=7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243954 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f04b25d-f38d-5fc1-9876-423c80368bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242439} {:answer/id #uuid "b15931fb-52e5-5c41-a258-369e7d1fb1c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242724} {:answer/id #uuid "b42567a6-9890-5794-8a22-d6d56c1dc629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242754} {:answer/id #uuid "d0121691-eca2-5974-80e3-dbeade97f6d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243013} {:answer/id #uuid "f9e06cb0-4838-5459-9758-b2749164bf96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b15931fb-52e5-5c41-a258-369e7d1fb1c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242724} :answer-field/id #uuid "e685e6a5-808d-5d60-91f6-26ddb332e292" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5dfc56d2-f4d4-58d9-9174-ebcc9a95025f" :question/math-academy-id "q-106781" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2+{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1-t+2{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=6+2t.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2+{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(1-t+2{t}^{2}) & =6+2t \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}t+({x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =6+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=6 \\\\ -{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=6 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{x}_{2} &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$  Substituting this into the first equation yields\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}+(-2)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+(-2)=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167307 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "446dabe3-49c3-5c19-a0ad-07eb84517536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -11 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559195} {:answer/id #uuid "7c777f84-b77f-5d85-8be5-0a060c689b19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559325} {:answer/id #uuid "946cf36a-cac6-5744-bff7-9916b58a2886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 6 & -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559384} {:answer/id #uuid "aa2453f1-9942-5ee6-8a23-474c9f7c5cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -6 \\\\ -11 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559442} {:answer/id #uuid "de8035ce-93fa-59c6-ab22-ecbea61f3db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "446dabe3-49c3-5c19-a0ad-07eb84517536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -11 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559195} :answer-field/id #uuid "2390925b-1353-541e-941f-543ca9985649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c1e13f4-dff1-54a4-a42b-6fe61fa7145e" :question/math-academy-id "q-36476" :question/problem "$$\n{A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Find the matrix $C$ given that $B=\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of the matrix $C$ relative to $B$ are $[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{A}_{1}+{x}_{2}{A}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]+(-3)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -15 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -11 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a03533aa-a487-5506-b27b-8c3bf79ec052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+2t-5{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359149} {:answer/id #uuid "a98b954a-62d7-5f9b-85ef-f9fbfe64dd5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+2t-6{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359211} {:answer/id #uuid "aa6200a4-46ff-597b-a52b-7de1bad06ec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+2t-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359217} {:answer/id #uuid "b1c82c40-c70c-5c5f-a09e-18f082e57213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+4t-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359299} {:answer/id #uuid "c49b3d79-b944-566f-804b-a42d9c9388d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1-3t-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa6200a4-46ff-597b-a52b-7de1bad06ec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=1+2t-{t}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359217} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b180e5f-8c33-58c8-b7dd-b3394e957bad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360169}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3bc8d8b-3247-5773-8b80-0a797bc2bf9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-95003" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1-t+2{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =1\\cdot (1-t+2{t}^{2})+3\\cdot (t-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =1-t+2{t}^{2}+3t-3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =1+2t-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22e3dfdc-803c-530b-828e-1f04c545062b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=-3t+2{t}^{2}-2{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559100} {:answer/id #uuid "47a215b1-2b3a-5000-bc50-233d09b9d4d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=-{t}^{2}+4{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559202} {:answer/id #uuid "4b7001e9-0338-5f47-b94a-debd241ffea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=-3t+2{t}^{2}+8{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559216} {:answer/id #uuid "8a74fc7a-d723-5249-bfd0-48d9b771d88b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=3t+6{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559363} {:answer/id #uuid "983d6858-aa25-5104-bc4a-bb5df7575f3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=3t+2{t}^{2}-2{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b7001e9-0338-5f47-b94a-debd241ffea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p(t)=-3t+2{t}^{2}+8{t}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559216} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a136902-a15d-512f-845b-8a048ae1d4bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71981b01-d421-5e25-8cb2-44a17e6d5470" :question/math-academy-id "q-95007" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=t-{t}^{3},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=2{t}^{2}+5{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =(-3)\\cdot (t-{t}^{3})+1\\cdot (2{t}^{2}+5{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =-3t+3{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}+5{t}^{3} \\\\  & =-3t+2{t}^{2}+8{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559880 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166751 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ab0ff2-ab0b-5d3f-9e26-734149456094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -8 \\\\ -5 & -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559188} {:answer/id #uuid "6151d1c3-f034-57e2-83b8-50371e7ef248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559260} {:answer/id #uuid "6f5c3abb-ee4d-5e86-90b9-f8fa0cd89cfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559292} {:answer/id #uuid "d9635e7a-2f1c-5ad8-bec3-9492822808ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}-13 & -8 \\\\ 5 & -15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559550} {:answer/id #uuid "ea265705-2964-5a34-9bb4-7e9db4a9c61a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6151d1c3-f034-57e2-83b8-50371e7ef248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559260} :answer-field/id #uuid "316ad55a-5e8d-586a-bd40-47b77c935abd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ee947d80-6aa8-5dc4-9785-d937ced374de" :question/math-academy-id "q-95010" :question/problem "$$\n{A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Find the matrix $C$ given that $B=\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\},$ and the coordinates of the matrix $C$ relative to $B$ are $[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\text{Span}\\{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{A}_{1}+{x}_{2}{A}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]+(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-9 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497380 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04ec09a2-fbda-5a52-bb47-467878875739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496666} {:answer/id #uuid "44cab1fc-6315-55b0-b3f7-05e725aa34f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496806} {:answer/id #uuid "68265195-74f6-5911-84af-be7e3b4820a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496883} {:answer/id #uuid "c58ad0a2-710d-5e98-bc14-5b4a2dc8be59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497061} {:answer/id #uuid "d1293524-2d61-50b9-9952-84c3ff0dc264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1293524-2d61-50b9-9952-84c3ff0dc264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497094} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fdc3716-f94a-5460-8503-fc942472a7e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497284}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8b164922-7a86-5e35-904e-baea511723b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-95012" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 9 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{B}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ -7 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 9 & 7\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ -7 & 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} & 6{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} \\\\ 9{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & 7{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ -7 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 6{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ 9{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-7 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2} &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 9 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 9 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{7}{6}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{13}{2} & -13 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{13}{6} & \\frac{13}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ -\\frac{13}{2}{x}_{2} &=-13 \\\\ \\frac{13}{6}{x}_{2} &=\\frac{13}{3}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second, third and fourth equations, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}+5\\cdot 2 & =4 \\\\ 6{x}_{1} & =-6 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1+2=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559870 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52f2bc5c-22ee-5401-83b8-a58e522c085f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559226} {:answer/id #uuid "767b5f1b-c79a-561a-9e70-43852522b78d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559314} {:answer/id #uuid "b9edf9cb-75a6-5e66-9a24-af4447fd7019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559479} {:answer/id #uuid "c40d1049-9690-549c-a325-1983d41ce8ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559498} {:answer/id #uuid "d505d171-6c9a-575c-8afc-95dad6d378eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52f2bc5c-22ee-5401-83b8-a58e522c085f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559226} :answer-field/id #uuid "53149fa6-8149-5883-9704-72bc13881279" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df9025d6-fcec-59a9-b2fb-091fd502413d" :question/math-academy-id "q-95014" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & -2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 & 3{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 12\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}=-10 \\\\ -9{x}_{2}=18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2(-2) & =-2 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2+(-2)=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5226adcf-c64d-5855-bb34-33692d805606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394992} {:answer/id #uuid "1218ec16-27de-5244-b46a-3719907959bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394993} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ba6bfb-aefb-5459-b3fb-9e2227499ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394994} {:answer/id #uuid "ff86cb35-663a-5979-afcf-39f451ff20d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394995} {:answer/id #uuid "d34c1e79-ae0a-5950-aeae-9c06b0734d12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1218ec16-27de-5244-b46a-3719907959bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394993} :answer-field/id #uuid "06578788-3100-5d6d-9df0-7305e2069e6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "afea1de7-9432-5f54-8eea-c94a31190309" :question/math-academy-id "q-95019" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{B}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $B={{B}_{1},{B}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}},$ and $[A]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} & -3{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 & -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ 9{x}_{2} &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5\\cdot 1 & =4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}+1=\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360540 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3aabddb-8f21-5ac4-85e0-911c0c8d8f98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359318} {:answer/id #uuid "baaa715b-7689-55ee-b14e-fd88568d265c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359375} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ea90f6-c8b2-51ad-92af-372a97869184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359502} {:answer/id #uuid "e785973e-4713-55d7-92da-c991e0d3c75b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359803} {:answer/id #uuid "e864d953-5e40-5d07-977c-588765dcc861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "baaa715b-7689-55ee-b14e-fd88568d265c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359375} :answer-field/id #uuid "b85ad7f6-b08d-59fb-bd7f-700836251219" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fd8162f1-9125-55c3-8d42-af30755391ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-95023" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1-{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=2+3t+4{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2+t)+{x}_{2}(1-{t}^{2}) & =2+3t+4{t}^{2} \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{1}t-{x}_{2}{t}^{2} & =2+3t+4{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{1} &=3 \\\\ -{x}_{2} &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-4.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}+(-4)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-4)=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "180fb67f-6a67-5314-a5a7-83e4f4288271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357961} {:answer/id #uuid "5273d4ec-0ed6-56c2-ad25-8714176aa52c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358460} {:answer/id #uuid "947b00dd-5c3a-5d68-97b8-f3e2c0d73d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359055} {:answer/id #uuid "a05b24ff-a2a2-55af-974a-b66d84b61f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359151} {:answer/id #uuid "e8e73b2f-7a58-5798-826f-d0fc8ea33b00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a05b24ff-a2a2-55af-974a-b66d84b61f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359151} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8fa47fa-89cb-527e-bbec-2ad37148ba17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d482ef0a-c05c-5115-aa27-a3051b991631" :question/math-academy-id "q-95030" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2{t}^{2}+t-2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}+3t-6,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=-2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2},\\,\\,q(t)=-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},$ then ${x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{t}^{2}+t-2)+{x}_{2}({t}^{2}+3t-6)+{x}_{3}(-2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}) & =-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6 \\\\ -2{x}_{3}{t}^{3}+(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+({x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})t+(-2{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}) & =-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{3} &=-2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=4 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2} &=-6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{3} &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-5{x}_{2}+3\\cdot 1=-2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3\\cdot 1=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},$ and therefore ${x}_{2}=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22ad037a-f496-5ab0-a932-5d46d0a21741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358051} {:answer/id #uuid "25191c8e-2e57-514d-a0e3-97eb11b38614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358084} {:answer/id #uuid "91079999-3ee4-51b4-8a41-eb5844424363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359024} {:answer/id #uuid "990978f8-3b62-5498-a322-63390ecdfc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359097} {:answer/id #uuid "f5416688-5725-590f-85f1-3ac8b46caa1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5416688-5725-590f-85f1-3ac8b46caa1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359925} :answer-field/id #uuid "93d9cdb7-1243-5677-ba45-c4f957c2881f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "03ea170e-d874-5ba1-a4f2-de4db0ee9679" :question/math-academy-id "q-95031" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=-{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=2{t}^{2}+4,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=3{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-3t+3,\\,\\,q(t)=-1.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},$ then ${x}_{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(-{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+t)+{x}_{2}(2{t}^{2}+4)+{x}_{3}(3{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-3t+3) & =-1 \\\\ (-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}){t}^{3}+({x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+({x}_{1}-3{x}_{3})t+(4{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}↔{R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -{x}_{3} &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n2{x}_{2}+2\\cdot 1=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-{x}_{1}+3\\cdot 1=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},$ and therefore ${x}_{3}=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366601 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8a372d3-d315-5749-addd-ca218934d8af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366603} {:answer/id #uuid "2ab3c27f-c881-553c-99a4-41fa0ef0a58d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366604} {:answer/id #uuid "28121894-e9ce-5b0a-806b-f6ec1501699f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366605} {:answer/id #uuid "78bb0746-d6c3-5d59-930f-936e9f2dd59b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366606} {:answer/id #uuid "8796c8c9-b669-522b-82ea-60854c0f52be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28121894-e9ce-5b0a-806b-f6ec1501699f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366605} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbc10d80-64bd-56a8-a6d8-b0abd6be83f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "63b1eaca-ad47-51c0-a706-057c6e426a92" :question/math-academy-id "q-95043" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=-6{t}^{3}+6t+12,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-3t-2,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=-3{t}^{2}+2t,\\,\\,q(t)=-9{t}^{3}+19t+18.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},$ then ${x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(-6{t}^{3}+6t+12)+{x}_{2}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-3t-2)+{x}_{3}(-3{t}^{2}+2t) & =-9{t}^{3}+19t+18 \\\\ (-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){t}^{3}+(-2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+(6{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})t+(12{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}) & =-9{t}^{3}+19t+18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-9 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 6{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=19 \\\\ 12{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=18.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 12 & -2 & 0 & 18\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 12 & -2 & 0 & 18\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-9 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{2}-3\\cdot 2=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-6{x}_{1}+(-3)=-9\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},$ and therefore ${x}_{2}=-3.$"}]}
